# Org-pack resolution (every chat)

This repo is generic and public. It never hardcodes a company name,
product, voice, or org chart. Any skill or doc reference to
`COMPANY-BUSINESS.md`, `COMPANY-VOICE.md`, `COMPANY-ARCHETYPES.md`,
`COMPANY-PATTERNS.md`, `COMPANY-SQUADS.md`, `COMPANY-SOURCES.md`,
`COMPANY-VOCABULARY.md`, or `COMPANY-STYLE-GUIDE.md` resolves in this
order:

1. `context/org-pack.local/COMPANY-*.md` — real company content, gitignored.
2. `context/org-pack/COMPANY-*.md` — public fictional "Northline" example,
   shipped with the harness as a fallback and a worked-example template.

**Read the local file when it exists; never mix the two** (don't fall
back to individual example files if the local pack exists but is
missing one file — flag the gap instead and ask, since a partial local
pack usually means a setup step didn't finish).

Full protocol: `harness/ORCHESTRATOR.md` §0a.

Any other `COMPANY-*.md` in the resolved folder is an **extra file**: read
its `about:` / `use-when:` header and load it when `use-when` matches the
skill or task (`harness/references/org-pack-extra-files.md`).

## Forbidden

- Hardcoding a specific company's name, product framing, or voice rules
  directly into `harness/ORCHESTRATOR.md`, any `harness/skills/**/SKILL.md`,
  or other engine files — those must reference the resolved `COMPANY-*.md`
  files instead.
- Writing real company facts into `context/org-pack/` (public folder).
- Treating a missing `context/org-pack.local/` as broken — it's the
  expected state on a fresh clone; fall back to the example pack silently.
